  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate and resource protection scholarship programme for young professionals from developing and emerging countries (phase III)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With this scholarship programme, Germany is promoting the training and development of prospective leaders  from emerging and developing countries who already have some expertise in the field of climate protection  and climate-relevant resource conservation. Working with recognised experts, they carry out scientific  projects in Germany relating to issues on the topic of climate protection and climate-relevant resource  conservation. The knowledge gained and the newly acquired methods are then transferred to the target  countries in order to support them in the battle against climate change and its effects. With the help of the  Humboldt Foundation&#x2019;s alumni work, long-term collaborations between the prospective leaders and German  as well as international partners are established. This will deepen and consolidate cooperation with specialist  colleagues in Germany over the long term.</narrative>
  </description>
